  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "do_fileid",
    "file": "opensc/src/pkcs15init/profile.c",
    "description": "`do_fileid` appends two file-ID bytes to `file->path.value` without unconditionally validating `path->len + 2` against the 16-byte path buffer. Its bounds check is incorrectly inside the parent-DF branch, so a root file with no parent bypasses it. In this PoV, a 16-byte `path` followed by `file-id =5501` overwrites the adjacent `path.len`, changing it from 16 to a large attacker-influenced value; a subsequent `file-id =340F` on the same reused `DF MF` performs a far out-of-bounds write into the `sc_file_t` ACL array. Cleanup then treats the corrupted ACL slot as a pointer and crashes while dereferencing it in `sc_file_clear_acl_entries`.",
    "conditions": "A parsed `filesystem` profile must create a root file (no parent) whose path is already at the 16-byte `SC_MAX_PATH_SIZE` limit, then apply a `file-id` command to it. Reopening/reusing the same file name (the PoV uses nested `DF MF`) and applying another valid two-byte `file-id` uses the corrupted `path.len` as the `memcpy` offset, allowing corruption within the `sc_file_t`; the supplied values corrupt an ACL pointer, which is dereferenced when profile parsing/finishing fails and `sc_profile_free` frees the file."
  },
